# Reference lab (.github/workflows/reference-lab.yml): what a push runs.
# The plan and its rules: BACKLOG §0 "Reference lab"; skill ui-design §4
# (MX is a reference for proportions and behaviour, never for looks).
#
# 28 Nov 2026 (3): SCREENS=subgest, the pinches. Run 46049383870: a
# swipe right steps back a line (L L R R R: 2 3 2 1 1); the band is the
# line's own box (60 px above the words stepped, 130 px was the seek); a
# 90 dp swipe steps (49 dp did not), on the finger's lift (a slow swipe
# had not stepped half way); a drag moves after ~60 px. Calibration failed
# again (display 0's panel, event2; the viewport read orientation 0
# sideways): mapping 0 — the axes following the turned screen — first now.
#
# 28 Nov 2026 (2): SCREENS=subgest again. Run 46047544023 (screens in
# innocent-ref): a swipe along the line (≥ ~200 dp, fast or slow, long or
# not, playing or paused, on the words or beside them in the line's
# full-width band) steps ONE line — right to left the next; ~50 dp did
# nothing; 260 px above the line it was the screen's seek. A drag moves the
# line with the finger after ~60 px of slop and MX keeps the place for the
# next film, showing "↕ N" at the top; the line gets a grey box while
# touched. No pinch: the touch panel taken was another display's (event11).
# Now: the previous line (L L R R R), where the band ends above the words
# (60 and 130 px), the shortest swipe that steps (90 and 140 dp), the
# pinches on display 0's panel, a short drag; the summary kept in the run.
#
# 28 Nov 2026: SCREENS=subgest — docs/handoff_2026_11_28_beyond_mx_p1.md,
# P5 (the owner wants MX's subtitle gestures, measured first). MX alone,
# sideways, a line of its .srt up and paused, from a fresh open each time:
# a swipe along the line (left, right, short, long, slow, beside the words,
# above the line, while playing), a drag up and down, a pinch out and in
# (two fingers by sendevent, the mapping found by a tap on ⋮). The
# summary: MX's subtitle box (its SubText views in the tree) and its
# position (media session) before and after each; screens to innocent-ref.
# Compare with Innocent's own (gestures/subtitle_band.dart,
# player_gesture_engine.dart: 64 dp a line, the band 6 % in from the sides).
#
# 27 Nov 2026: SCREENS=fps — docs/handoff_2026_11_27_beyond_mx.md P2/P3.
# Does MX 3.4.3 vote the film's frame rate (Surface.setFrameRate on its
# layer) or ask its window for a display mode or refresh rate? The 24 fps
# measuring film sideways in each app, 12 s in; SurfaceFlinger's dump and
# the window's attributes (to innocent-ref), the votes' values in the
# summary. Innocent today: no vote on its own surface (its ExoPlayer votes
# on an ImageReader no display shows; libmpv none).
#
# 22 Nov 2026: fetch the MX Player the owner has on the phone (installed
# from the Play Store, version 3.4.3, read off the phone's App info) and keep
# it in the private repository innocent-ref. Nothing to compare with yet.
#   run 44984807250: innocent-ref reached (private); listed Google Play,
