# 22 Nov 2026 (later): MODE=probe — does MX 3.4.3 (native code for
# arm64-v8a only) run on an x86_64 image that translates ARM? First
# google_apis API 30 (Android 11), where Innocent's own libs once died on a
# SIMD instruction inside libndk_translation; another translating API if
# not. Sized like the owner's phone (1080x2316, 450 dpi, three-button nav,
# punch hole); MX's network cut by uid; our own measuring film. Compare
# with nothing yet: this run says whether Phase 1 can use the emulator.
#   run 44989031141: MX 3.4.3 INSTALLS on API 30 (base, arm64 split,
#     xxxhdpi; primary ABI arm64-v8a under translation). The film's intent
#     with -p brought Android's "Open with" chooser (MX has a player and a
#     pop-up player) and MX never ran. Run 2 names the player activity.
#   run 44989696334: MX's native code loads through the translator
#     ("Initialized NDK translation (aarch64)"), no SIGILL. But it opened the
#     PiP activity (first by name) and MX showed its own storage screen
#     (READ_EXTERNAL_STORAGE alone is not enough for it); the first-run
#     tapper chose its "not now" and MX left. Run 3: the player activity in
#     Android's order, not pop-up/PiP; "All files access" allowed (appops).
#   run 44990303466: PHASE 0 PASSES. MX's player (ActivityScreen) opened
#     the film offline, controls up, resumed 1, alive 1, SIGILL 0, fatal 0;
#     779 packets MX tried were refused (the uid cut holds). MX turned
#     itself sideways. uiautomator never found MX's player idle (10 s
